      "message": "[warning] Line 36: 🟡 `started(conversationId:)` always removes the first queued deadline, but expired deadlines are never pruned. If older requests have already timed out, a new upload can consume an expired slot and leave a valid pending request behind, which keeps the extension running longer than needed. Prune expired entries before consuming one (or pass current uptime into `started` and remove the first unexpired deadline).",
